\begin{lemma}\label{l:l22}
	Let $k = n^{\Omega(1)}$ and $k \ge s^7$. If an $n$-vertex orientation $G$ with $\alpha(G) < s$ and $\alpha^*(G) < s$ has at least $(k/se)^k$ acyclic $k$-sets, then it has a set of $n' \ge k^{2-o(1)}/s$ vertices inducing a $q$-almost-acyclic subgraph $G'$
