ref_dict.thm_sant:
\begin{theorem}[Functional Santal\'o inequality] \label{thm_sant}
Let $f,g$ be non-negative measurable functions on $\R^n$
satisfying
\begin{equation} \label{eq_sant} 
f(x)g(y)\leq \e^{-x\cdot y} , \quad \forall x,y\in\R^n .
\end{equation}
If $f$ (or $g$) has its barycenter at $0$, namely if $\int_{\R^n} x f(x) \, dx = 0$,
then 
\[ 
\int_{\R^n} f(x) \, dx \int_{\R^n} g(y) \, dy \leq  (2\pi)^n . 
\]   
\end{theorem}

